Q1. What is the purpose of assigning a specific name to a Docker container using the --name option?

Interview Ready Answer

The --name option assigns a custom, human-readable name to a Docker
container. It allows Docker commands such as docker stop, docker start,
docker exec, and docker logs to reference the container by name instead
of its container ID.

Definition

--name
- Assigns a custom name to a container.
- Replaces the need to remember the container ID.

Purpose

• Easily identify containers.
• Manage containers using meaningful names.
• Improves readability in projects with multiple containers.

======================================================================

Q2. What is Detached Mode (-d)?

Interview Ready Answer

Detached mode (-d) runs a Docker container in the background. After the
container starts, Docker immediately returns control of the terminal to
the user while the container continues running.

Definition

Detached Mode
- Background execution mode.
- Terminal is released immediately.
- Container keeps running.

Purpose

• Run web servers.
• Run databases.
• Run backend services continuously.
• Continue using the terminal after starting the container.

Real-Life Example

Spring Boot Application
↓
docker run -d
↓
Application keeps running
↓
Terminal becomes available for other commands

