Q3. What is Interactive Mode (-it)?

Interview Ready Answer

Interactive mode (-it) allows the user to interact with a running Docker
container through a terminal.

It combines:

-i
Keeps STDIN open.

-t
Allocates a pseudo-terminal (TTY).

Definition

Interactive Mode
- Opens an interactive shell.
- Allows manual command execution inside the container.

Purpose

• Debug applications.
• Inspect container files.
• Execute Linux commands inside the container.
• Troubleshoot running containers.

Real-Life Example

Ubuntu Container
↓
Run with -it
↓
Access Linux shell
↓
Execute commands manually

