Q4. Why do we publish container ports using the -p option?

Interview Ready Answer

The -p option maps a host machine port to a container port, allowing
applications running inside the container to be accessed from outside
the container.

Definition

Port Mapping
Host Port  →  Container Port

Purpose

• Expose containerized applications.
• Access web applications from a browser.
• Enable communication between the host and the container.

Real-Life Example

Spring Boot runs on port 8080 inside the container.

Host Port 8080
        │
        ▼
Container Port 8080

Browser
↓
http://localhost:8080

