Q5. What is the purpose of the --rm option?

Interview Ready Answer

The --rm option automatically removes a Docker container after it exits.
It is mainly used for temporary or one-time containers to prevent stopped
containers from accumulating.

Definition

--rm
- Automatic container removal after exit.

Purpose

• Keep the system clean.
• Avoid unused stopped containers.
• Useful for temporary containers.

